From 61b93cff7900b24c17011d481fd6c31f5abb59e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bradley Gleave <bradley@bradleytgpcoaching.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 18:23:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(importer): page and write the ledger by composite
 provenance identity

Readers: roster and entity pages now order by (source_id, source_platform)
and issue a v2 cursor carrying both. A legacy cursor is resolved by one
in-scope lookup; when it names exactly one canonical row the page is
identical, otherwise it is the existing 400 'malformed cursor' and the
client restarts from the first page. Cursors minted by the R readers are
rejected the same way; there is no fallback.

Writer: the reconstruction ledger requires source_platform and the upsert
targets the five-field identity; a repeated unique violation under
contention surfaces as 409 'reconstruction provenance conflict'. No
migration ships: the NOT NULL column and both identity keys already exist.

Contract version label 2.0.0-c1-s1.2; OpenAPI regenerated.

Real-PG proof (test-only, run only through jest.rls.config.js): the sixth
disposable identity g2_nq1_disposable on port 55481 with a T root at the
accepted R head, cases N01-N06 and Q01-Q07, plus the DB-free guard spec.
